**Finding: missing (LOL-CAP, critical)**

The Agreement contains no limitation of liability of any kind. I swept for "liability", "consequential", "in no event", "damages" and "indemnif", and read the General Provisions (§10), Warranties (§9), Confidentiality (§8) and the signature block. The only "liability" references are in §10.2 (no joint venture), which are unrelated. There is no cap, no damages exclusion and no carve-out framework, so both parties — including the Company — carry unlimited exposure, failing both the preferred and fallback positions.

Redline (validated, `ok:true`): new **§10.9 Limitation of Liability** inserted after §10.8, at the preferred position:
- mutual cap at the greater of twelve months' fees paid or payable by the Company and USD 1,000,000;
- mutual exclusion of indirect, incidental, special, consequential and punitive damages;
- uncapped "Excluded Claims" (confidentiality, data protection/security, indemnification, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud, infringement of the other party's IP);
- confirmation that the Company's payment obligations under §3 and the §4.2 Termination Payment are not capped "damages".

Fallback if HDI pushes back: drop the USD 1,000,000 floor to a straight twelve months' fees cap, retaining at least the indemnification, confidentiality, gross negligence and wilful misconduct carve-outs.
